# Managed by kwisatz tasks/setup-tensorfold-spark-qwen38-27b.sh. A re-run
# updates only the keys this file owns (FOREGROUND, PORT, HOST) and keeps every
# other line you added (mode 600).
# Upstream scripts/config.sh reads this file (the environment wins over it).
# Note: TENSORFOLD_MEMORY_RESERVE_GIB defaults to 0 here; Flash Next keeps 10.
# FOREGROUND=1: start.sh blocks for the container's lifetime, which is the
# process llama-swap tracks as the model's cmd. PORT: TensorFold's fixed
# host-network port (llama-swap proxies to http://127.0.0.1:<PORT>; 8889 —
# Flash Next holds 8888).
# Engine levers (PARALLEL, CONTEXT, YARN_FACTOR, KV_POOL_GB, KV_DTYPE,
# PREFILL_FP8, VISION, DRAFT_ID, TENSORFOLD_*) can be added here;
# see /srv/tensorfold-27b/scripts/config.sh.
FOREGROUND=1
PORT=${PORT}
# Loopback only: the API is consumed through llama-swap (which proxies to
# 127.0.0.1) — no unauthenticated direct LAN access to the raw endpoint.
HOST=127.0.0.1
